-- title:
--   Inverse Frobenius twist with its Verschiebung and relative Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $\pi\in\mathcal O$ an element with $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$, let $O^{nr}$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, and assume: the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $O^{nr}$ is maximal; every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{nr}$ has a root modulo that ideal; and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo that ideal for all $x\in O^{nr}$. Write $k_0:=O^{nr}/(\pi)$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$, let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ and let $A_0$ be a fake elliptic curve over $k_0$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ data. Then there exist a fake elliptic curve $A_0^{(1/r)}$ over $k_0$ and a morphism $\mathrm{pr}_A:A_0^{(1/r)}\to A_0$ exhibiting $A_0^{(1/r)}$ as the base change of $A_0$ along the ring map $k_0\to k_0$ induced by $\mathrm{Fr}^{-1}$, in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullbackVia`: the square formed by $\mathrm{pr}_A$, the two structure morphisms and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of that ring map is a pullback, $\mathrm{pr}_A$ carries the group law on $T$-points to the group law over the base change, it intertwines the $\Lambda$-actions, and points of $A_0^{(1/r)}$ factoring through its level scheme are carried to points of $A_0$ factoring through $A_0$'s level scheme; and there exist morphisms $F:A_0\to A_0^{(1/r)}$ and $V:A_0^{(1/r)}\to A_0$ over $k_0$ such that: for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k_0$, composition with $F$ and with $V$ is a homomorphism for the relative group laws on $T$-points; $F$ and $V$ commute with the $\Lambda$-actions, i.e. $F\circ\mathrm{act}_{A_0}(x)=\mathrm{act}_{A_0^{(1/r)}}(x)\circ F$ and $V\circ\mathrm{act}_{A_0^{(1/r)}}(x)=\mathrm{act}_{A_0}(x)\circ V$ for all $x\in\Lambda$; both carry points factoring through the respective level scheme to points factoring through the other level scheme; on $T$-points $V\circ F$ and $F\circ V$ are both the $r$-fold iterated sum for the respective group law; and for every commutative ring $C$ of characteristic $r$ and every $x:\operatorname{Spec}C\to A_0^{(1/r)}$ one has $V\circ x=\mathrm{pr}_A\circ x\circ\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Frob}_C)$, where $\mathrm{Frob}_C$ is the $r$-th power map on $C$.
--
--   This provides, over the residue field $k_0=O^{nr}/(\pi)$, the Frobenius–Verschiebung pair attached to the inverse Frobenius twist $A_0^{(1/r)}$ of a fake elliptic curve, with $V$ (not $F$) identified as the relative Frobenius of the twist over $\mathrm{pr}_A$, and with all compatibilities with the quaternionic action and the level-$N$ data recorded. It is used in the construction of rigidifications whose Frobenius twist is acted on by a scalar, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison.
